      "definition": "Pemphigus vulgaris is a chronic autoimmune blistering disease in which antibodies disrupt adhesion between epidermal keratinocytes. It typically begins with painful oral erosions and can cause fragile, flaccid skin blisters and widespread erosions; infection, fluid loss, malnutrition, and immunosuppressive-treatment toxicity create the major safety burden.",
