      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-02",
      "definition": "Primary ciliary dyskinesia is a usually inherited disorder of motile-cilia structure, function, or assembly. Ineffective mucociliary clearance causes chronic upper- and lower-airway infection and inflammation from infancy, while related cilia and flagella defects can alter organ laterality, hearing, and fertility.",
